# A head whose fallback element is itself a comprehension: both conditions false leave the list empty.
-- source.cue --
o!: int
p!: int
-- target.cue --
n!: int
-- lens.cue --
input: _
result: {
	n: [if input.o == 1 {input.o}, if input.p == 1 {input.p}][0]
}
-- out --
unknown
result.n takes the first element of a list built by if input.o == 1 whose fallback is itself conditional, so when the conditions are false the list is empty and the index fails; add an unconditional fallback element: [if c {x}, y][0] (rule unknown-head) @ lens.cue:3:5
